# Real personal data: student's GitHub username and repo names (BUILD_PLAN 1.2). The
# template, config/roster.example.yaml, stays tracked -- same split as .env/.env.example.
config/roster.yaml
config/roster.yaml.bak
config/roster.yaml.tmp

# Internal source-of-truth design documents and generated explainer. Kept locally as
# the authority every formula in variables/ is transcribed from and reviewed against,
# but not meant for the public repo.
BUILD_PLAN.md
CLAUDE.md
VDEL_Modules_1_2_Build.md
VDEL_Modules_3_9_Build.md
VDEL_v1_Execution_Plan.md
VDEL_REDESIGN.md
vdel_complete_design_document.md
SETUP.md
EXECUTION.md
.claude/

*.bak

# docs/ is TRACKED (D-105). Until then the directory was ignored wholesale with a short allow-list,
# so most documents never entered git. These stay local on purpose; each is either personal,
# rewritten every session, or a disposable cache:
#   STATUS.md            the author's milestone board with pasted run output (note: it was already
#                        added to git while it was allow-listed; ignoring it does not untrack it)
#   FRAMEWORK_STATUS.md  the author's private framework notes
#   HANDOFF.md           one session, overwritten at every session end
#   reading/             compressed reads, valid "until the code changes"
#   *OVERNIGHT_REPORT.md batch reports kept local on purpose (agents branch, v1 batch)
#   design/              the redesign document, listed as "not meant for the public repo" above
# docs/FINALIZE_PROGRESS.md is deliberately NOT here: it is how a new session resumes the work.
docs/STATUS.md
docs/FRAMEWORK_STATUS.md
docs/HANDOFF.md
docs/reading/
docs/*OVERNIGHT_REPORT.md
docs/design/

# Local scratch at the repo root: one-off DB queries and a manual Code Agent driver.
# Neither is part of any deliverable, and neither is worth promoting to scripts/ -- they
# exist to be edited and thrown away. Ignored rather than deleted so they stay available
# locally without ever entering a diff or the lint gate.
exec.py
check_assignments.py

# scripts/render_student_repo.py's durable output location. A rendered repo is a
# GENERATED artifact -- it is real, but it is derived entirely from `curriculum/master/`
# plus the DB (gaps, variants, the student's mastery), the same "raw tables are the
# source of truth, not what's derived from them" rule the rest of this project already
# follows for `attempts`/`variants` themselves. Re-running the render reproduces it byte
# for byte from those real sources; committing it would mean tracking a byte-for-byte
# reproducible copy of files this repo already tracks (the master files) alongside
# per-student content (a real student's code, once they start editing it) that has no
# business in the instructor's own repo history at all.
renders/

# benchmark/run_benchmark.py's own durable output -- a real run's per-call results
# (including any call_errors), written so a finding like D-050's quota exhaustion
# survives the process exiting even when --commit is never passed. Reproducible from a
# live LLM call each time, same reasoning as renders/ above -- not source, not tracked.
benchmark/results/

# pg_dump backups of the dev database (real student data -- names, code, traces). Taken
# before destructive migrations such as scripts/normalise_test_names.py --apply.
backups/

# agents/budget.py's local per-day LLM call ledger (counts only, no content)
.vdel/

# run_hourly.py logs (scripts/run_hourly.py, D-091): one file per day, 14 days kept
logs/
